course: dictionary
lesson: 3895
title: Friars and friends in the story
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A friar is a man who belongs to a Christian religious order, and he has promised to live simply. You can often work out the meaning from the clues around the word. «The Spanish friar Bernardino de Sahagún recorded Aztec memories» tells you a friar is a man who writes and records things, and that he is part of a church group.
explain: Look at the word before a name. «Friar Tuck» and «the friar Bartolomé de las Casas» both put friar in front of a man's name, the way a title such as Doctor or Captain does. Ask yourself: what kind of man is this? A friar is a religious man who travels among people.
explain: Friars are not quite the same as monks. A monk mostly stays in one monastery, but a friar goes out into towns to preach, teach and help the poor. Swap the word into a sentence, and check: does «a friar walked into the town to help the poor» make sense? If yes, you have the right idea.
fact: A friar is a man who belongs to a Christian religious order.
fact: Friars promise to live simply and travel among people.
fact: Friars go out into towns to preach, teach and help the poor.
fact: Monks mostly stay in a monastery, but friars travel out into the world.
fact: «Friar» is used as a title before a name, as in «Friar Tuck», the jolly friar in the Robin Hood stories.
exercise: «The friar walked from town to town to help the poor.» What is a friar? | *A man in a Christian religious order who travels to help people | A kind of horse | A farmer who grows wheat | A king who ruled a town
exercise: In «Friar Tuck», what does the word friar tell you? | *It is a title used before a man's name | It is a bird that sings | It means a fast runner | It means a feast
exercise: What is the difference between a monk and a friar? | Monks go out into towns to preach, and friars stay in a monastery | *Monks mostly stay in a monastery, but friars go out into towns to preach and help the poor | There is no difference at all | Monks always wear a crown
test: «The Spanish friar Bernardino de Sahagún recorded Aztec memories of the conquest.» What is the best meaning of friar here? | A ruler of a Spanish city | *A religious man who belongs to a Christian order | A soldier who fights battles | A merchant who sells cloth
test: «Friar Tuck is the jolly friar in Robin Hood.» Which clue tells you friar is a title? | *It comes before a name | It is in a story | It has a capital letter at the start of the sentence only | It is a long word
exam: «The friar Bartolomé de las Casas wrote fiercely against cruelty.» Which word means the same as preach? | *Speak out to teach people about faith | Dance | Sleep | Trade
